### SeatGrid API examples — click "Send Request" (VS Code REST Client extension)
@base = http://localhost:8080

### Health: which coordinator answered, is it the leader? (send several times)
GET {{base}}/health

### Cluster: shard map, replication lag, circuit breakers, leader
GET {{base}}/api/cluster

### Text search + filters + sort (served by ONE replica; availability from Redis)
GET {{base}}/api/events?q=karachi&maxPrice=2500&sort=availability&order=desc

### Partial-word search (trigram index)
GET {{base}}/api/events?q=qalan&sort=price

### One match: free seats per section (scatter-gather over every shard)
GET {{base}}/api/events/1

### Live seat map of one section (Redis bitmap)
GET {{base}}/api/events/1/sections/5/seats

### Is a username free? (Ring B -> one owner shard, constant time)
GET {{base}}/api/auth/username-available?username=demo

### Register
POST {{base}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "fan_one", "email": "fan@example.com", "password": "password123" }

### Log in (seeded users: demo, admin, user0000001 ... — password "password123")
# @name login
POST {{base}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "demo", "password": "password123" }

###
@token = {{login.response.body.token}}

### My profile and wallet
GET {{base}}/api/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Step 1a: hold specific seats (send twice: the second gets 409 "Seat already taken")
# @name hold
POST {{base}}/api/holds
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "eventId": 1, "sectionId": 5, "seatNos": [10, 11] }

### Step 1b: or hold the best available N seats (SKIP LOCKED)
POST {{base}}/api/holds
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "eventId": 1, "sectionId": 12, "quantity": 3 }

### Step 2: pay (2PC: seat shard + user shard). Send twice: same key -> same tickets, no double charge.
POST {{base}}/api/bookings
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "eventId": 1, "sectionId": 5, "holdId": "{{hold.response.body.holdId}}", "idempotencyKey": "demo-order-0001" }

### My tickets (user_tickets index on my own shard)
GET {{base}}/api/me/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Ticket lookup: the number encodes event + section -> routed straight to one shard
GET {{base}}/api/tickets/E001-S05-0010-ABCD

### ---------------- Admin (log in as "admin") ----------------
# @name adminLogin
POST {{base}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "admin", "password": "password123" }

###
@admin = {{adminLogin.response.body.token}}

### Sales per match and class (partial SUM/COUNT per shard, merged)
GET {{base}}/api/admin/sales
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}

### Bookings by username prefix across all shards (top-K per shard + K-way merge, keyset paging)
GET {{base}}/api/admin/bookings?username=demo&limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}

### Consistency verifier
GET {{base}}/api/admin/verify
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}

### 2PC log + prepared transactions on each shard
GET {{base}}/api/admin/transactions
Authorization: Bearer {{admin}}
